Now the lease atomicity fix in store.js. Current:

```js
  async acquireLease(name, holderId, ttlMs) {
    const current = await this.getMeta(`lease:${name}`);
    const now = Date.now();
    if (current && current.expiresAt > now && current.holderId !== holderId) return false;
    await this.setMeta(`lease:${name}`, { holderId, expiresAt: now + ttlMs, acquiredAt: new Date(now).toISOString() });
    return true;
  }
```

`getMeta` and `setMeta` are async but contain only sync SQL. The await points allow interleaving across concurrent DO requests. Change to direct synchronous SQL within one async function (no awaits):

```js
  async acquireLease(name, holderId, ttlMs) {
    const key = `lease:${name}`;
    const row = this.sql.exec('SELECT value FROM meta WHERE key = ?', key).toArray()[0];
    const current = row ? JSON.parse(row.value) : null;
    const now = Date.now();
    if (current && current.expiresAt > now && current.holderId !== holderId) return false;
    this.sql.exec(
      `INSERT INTO meta (key, value) VALUES (?, ?) ON CONFLICT(key) DO UPDATE SET value = excluded.value`,
      key, JSON.stringify({ holderId, expiresAt: now + ttlMs, acquiredAt: new Date(now).toISOString() })
    );
    return true;
  }
```

Since there is no await, the read-check-write is one synchronous run-to-completion block in the DO. Also `releaseLease` sets null; same shape.

Note DO SQLite `sql.exec()` is synchronous — yes, per Cloudflare docs.

