No retailer list. Lavazza IL isn't an e-commerce partner directory. Vendor #3 via this route is a dead end; the existing docs already record research blockers generally. I could add a note in SOURCES.md about the additional candidates checked today (lavazza.co.il brand site without checkout; coffee-point.co.il Wix; search engines blocked from the runner) to keep the research record honest and useful for the next iteration. That's cheap and valuable.

Let me append to the "Sources researched and not included" table:
| lavazza.co.il | Official IL brand site; product pages are content only (no price, cart or shipping) | Not an e-commerce source. |
| coffeepoint.co.il | Wix store; server-rendered HTML has no stable product/price data and shipping is only calculated at checkout | No reliable structured product page from the runner. |
| Search engines (Bing/DDG HTML) | DDG returned challenge pages (202); Bing's result targets were not extractable | Used to look for further IL vendors without success. |

Wait — is documenting search engines as a "source" appropriate? It's research notes; fine. Keep it concise and truthful.

Then commit/push. After that, I think the session's work is complete and verified. But the instruction says to keep going until the task objective is fully achieved. The task is an ongoing loop; the objective (build the site) is achieved and Ready for handoff. Continuing to add marginal value is good but we should also consider the risk of breaking things. I'll add the research note, do a final full verification, and then consider whether anything else is worth doing.

Other small improvements worth considering:
1. `public/index.html` has `<div id="footer-status">` never used by app.js (footer status rendered into `#board`). Dead element — harmless. Could remove or wire it. Minor hygiene: remove the unused div? `renderFooterStatus` appends to board. The static footer status text "Waiting for the first refresh." stays forever. That's a small UI inconsistency: the footer says "Waiting for the first refresh." even after loading. Let me check: index.html `<footer class="site-footer"><div id="footer-status" class="site-footer__status">Waiting for the first refresh.</div></footer>`. app.js renders freshness in the board's meta-line, not into #footer-status. So the visible footer permanently claims "Waiting for the first refresh." That's misleading once data loads. Fix: have app.js update `#footer-status` with the last refresh time, or remove the element. Better: update it in `renderFooterStatus` or in `render()`:
```js
const footerStatus = document.getElementById('footer-status');
if (footerStatus) footerStatus.textContent = boardData.freshness?.lastRefreshAt ? `Board refreshed ${timeLabel(boardData.freshness.lastRefreshAt)}` : 'No completed refresh yet.';
```
And on error: 'Board unavailable.' This is a real, visible correctness fix. Add a QA check for it (footer status matches freshness). Let me implement.

2. `state.showUnknown` from URL: `unknown=0` hides; fine.

3. `renderControls` adds destination change listener only when dataset.ready unset; fine.

Let me implement the footer status fix + QA check. Small and verifiable.

Edit app.js render():
```js
function render() {
  renderControls();
  updateFooterStatus();
  ...
}
function updateFooterStatus() {
  const node = document.getElementById('footer-status');
  if (!node) return;
  if (state.error) { node.textContent = 'The board could not be loaded; the last stored data is shown above when available.'; return; }
  const last = state.board?.freshness?.lastRefreshAt;
  node.textContent = last ? `Last completed refresh: ${timeLabel(last)}. Vendor checks are listed above the footer.` : 'No completed refresh yet; the first scheduled run will populate the board.';
}
```
Hmm, `timeLabel` returns e.g. "12 Oct 2026, 14:49 (just now)". Fine.

QA check: in desktop evaluate, capture `footerStatus: document.getElementById('footer-status')?.textContent`; check it doesn't include 'Waiting for the first refresh' and includes 'Last completed refresh' when API freshness.lastRefreshAt exists. In fixtures mode lastRefreshAt = server `now` → present. In live mode present too. Good.

Then run offline QA (expect 35 checks), commit, push.

Let me apply.

